       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg add little blood pressure benefit and raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia. Your patient's profile (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) doesn't call for a higher dose.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the maximum standard dose, and I can enter it now.\n- **Add a second agent.** If 10 mg isn't enough, an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic is usually the next step. I can enter that order if you tell me the drug and dose.\n- **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily, as written.** If you want this on purpose, confirm it and I'll enter it with a note saying the dose is above the usual maximum and was intentional.\n\nWhich would you like?"
